            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0163" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.927/105: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Howell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-04-07T11:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 7—10:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>11. Your instruction number 249, February 2nd and subsequent correspondence. Am
                    only today advised both British and French representatives approve draft of
                    note. Shall I present draft transmitted by Department? Believe Egyptian
                    Government likely to accede.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
